From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:25:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 41/59] hjviewer: every Android build is controller-only

A phone or tablet with HJViewer controls PCs and is never controlled
(decision D1, option B' of the Google Play design 3-3). Without the
accessibility service and the foreground services Google Play asks for no
declaration beyond a privacy policy, and the side-loaded APK and the Play
bundle stay one variant.

- The manifest no longer declares InputService (accessibility), MainService
  (foreground service: specialUse, mediaProjection, microphone),
  FloatingWindowService and BootReceiver, nor the permissions only they
  used: FOREGROUND_SERVICE and its three types, SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW,
  REQUEST_IGNORE_BATTERY_OPTIMIZATIONS and RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED. The
  accessibility service's configuration and the two strings of the removed
  entries go with them. RECORD_AUDIO stays for a voice call started on the
  phone; the QR scanner's plugin still brings CAMERA.
- hjviewer.rs sets the hard setting conn-type to "outgoing" on Android, in a
  build without HJV_SERVER too, since the manifest is the same there.
  Upstream then leaves out the "Chat" and "Share screen" tabs and, in the
  settings, Deploy, Disable UDP, 2FA, "Share screen", "Enhancements" and
  the recording of incoming sessions. Those are all the places that started
  or stopped the services, opened the accessibility settings, asked for the
  overlay and battery permissions or kept the start-on-boot switch.
- MainActivity.onStart stops FloatingWindowService at every start. Android
  documents a SecurityException for a service that cannot be found, so the
  call is caught. Nothing else reaches a removed component: MainActivity
  binds MainService and starts the floating window only when
  MainService.isReady, which only a running MainService sets, and
  "init_service" is only sent from the "Share screen" tab or after a running
  MainService reported itself.
- A voice call records with the microphone permission, and the "Share
  screen" tab was the one place that asked for it. The "Voice call" menu of
  a session now asks itself (hjviewer_android.dart): it says why with the
  existing config_microphone text, shows Android's prompt, and requests the
  call once the permission is there. Other platforms call as before.

The Kotlin classes of the removed components stay in the tree, unreachable,
and PermissionRequestTransparentActivity stays declared: MainActivity and
MainService refer to them, and taking them out would change more of
upstream's files for no difference in the app.

Tests: conn-type as set here is what upstream's is_outgoing_only() reads; a
voice call asks for the microphone it lacks and is not made when it is
refused; the manifest declares nothing of the controlled side and keeps
RECORD_AUDIO.

Known limits: "Show terminal extra keys" is in the hidden "Enhancements"
section, so it stays as it was set (shown by default); iOS never had the
switch. Android tells the app only when the microphone is allowed, and a
refusal ends as the request's two-minute timeout, so the notice comes with
the prompt, not after a refusal. If the permission is gone by the time the
PC accepts the call (a one-time grant that lapsed in the background), the
call fails with upstream's message, which still points to the hidden
"Share screen" page; pressing "Voice call" again asks for the permission.
(A permission taken back in Android's settings ends the app's process, and
with it the session.) A voice call records while HJViewer
is on screen: the microphone foreground service went with MainService, as
it was for a phone that never started screen sharing. Kotlin and the
manifest are not built on the development machine: the first Android
build and a device check them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
